WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.440
What can Joe Biden get done without the Senate?&nbsp;
As I've mentioned a dozen times this week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.880
control of the Senate is not yet determined. There&nbsp;
are two run off Senate races in Georgia, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:21.040
will happen on January 5th. We'll be covering&nbsp;
them very extensively. If Democrats get both,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:27.600
it will be 50/50, making Kamala Harris as vice&nbsp;
president the tie breaking vote. Democrats could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:33.440
effectively control the Senate, but the question&nbsp;
is, without the Senate, what can get done? Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.760
go through it. First of all, there's a long list&nbsp;
of executive orders. A lot of the disasters Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.280
Trump got us into with executive orders, he can&nbsp;
get us out of anything Trump did unilaterally.&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.840
Joe Biden can undo unilaterally. And we've already&nbsp;
talked about getting back into Paris climate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.040
getting back into the show, getting rid&nbsp;
of the military trans ban, reinstating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.920
the Dreamer program, doing a lot with&nbsp;
covid. And he's already launched a task&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.560
force. There's tons of agency stuff. You&nbsp;
know, Trump has reorient reoriented the EPA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.600
to be weak. Joe Biden could reorient the EPA&nbsp;
to be stronger to protect the environment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.760
NASA was directed to stop studying climate. Joe&nbsp;
Biden can get NASA to be studying climate again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.400
So there is quite a bit that Joe Biden can do&nbsp;
foreign policy. Biden can do a lot of a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.840
foreign policy things that aren't budgetary and&nbsp;
thus need to go through the House and Senate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:32.000
But there's a lot of foreign policy. Fixing&nbsp;
relationships, fixing a bunch of the trade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.960
stuff with China, if China is willing, maybe&nbsp;
getting us back into the Iran nuclear deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.640
a lot of that can be done without controlling&nbsp;
the Senate. The stuff that will be difficult is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.200
you know, infrastructure, including green&nbsp;
infrastructure. You need the House and Senate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:54.640
tax reform, real health care reform. You're&nbsp;
going to need the House and Senate for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:01.200
unless you make deals with the devil, essentially,&nbsp;
unless you make compromises that I can't imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.160
Joe Biden would want to do. And that would be&nbsp;
sort of my one area of of caution, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.960
it's great for Joe Biden to talk about. I will be&nbsp;
the president. Whether you voted for me or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.960
I will be the president of the United&nbsp;
States, not just of blue states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.240
rather than red states. It's great that Joe Biden&nbsp;
is saying that. It's great that Joe Biden is, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:25.040
know, a guy who has been able to work across the&nbsp;
aisle. These people are disgusting, though, these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.960
Republicans. And the idea that you're going to get&nbsp;
your agenda done with their help is ridiculous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:38.960
You could maybe get Pyrrhic victories. The idea of&nbsp;
a Pyrrhic victory is you win, but you do so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.600
self-inflicted damage and winning that you end&nbsp;
up wondering, is that really a win anymore? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.600
the way that would work out as a Pyrrhic victory&nbsp;
would be you get something done on paper, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:55.680
compromises you make damage the country in such&nbsp;
a way that it ends up being a wash, for example.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:01.200
I think that's the risk of Joe Biden. I think&nbsp;
there would be a naivete if Joe Biden really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.680
thinks he's going to work with these clowns.&nbsp;
My hope is and I don't pretend to know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.520
we'll see. And if it doesn't go this&nbsp;
way, we'll criticize Biden. My hope&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:17.120
is that Biden is using language of uniting the&nbsp;
American people, but he is not naively thinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.640
he's going to get a lot of this big stuff done by&nbsp;
working with Republicans because they're just not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.720
going to work with him in any way. That would&nbsp;
approximate what we would call a leftward move.&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.160
It remains to be seen. I'm not putting the&nbsp;
cart before the horse. I will criticize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:39.040
it if it happens. But I am going to hope and&nbsp;
lobby that Joe Biden accurately understands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.800
that these are not people that you can negotiate&nbsp;
with or that you can bargain with because you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:50.160
will just damage yourself. That's my sense&nbsp;
right now. I'd love to hear your thoughts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

